Privacy Policy

Effective Date: 4/10/2026

Scam Check (“we”, “our”, or “us”) operates the Scam Check Android application (the “App”).
This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our App.

By using the App, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.

1. Information We Collect
a. Information You Provide

The App may collect the following information when you use it:

Shop or business name

Product details (names, prices, quantities, stock levels)

Sales and inventory records

Supplier or customer names (if entered by the user)

This data is entered voluntarily by the user to manage shop and inventory operations.

b. Automatically Collected Information

We may automatically collect:

Device information (device model, OS version)

App usage data (screens visited, features used)

Crash logs and performance data

This data is used solely to improve app stability and performance.

c. Personal Information

The App does not require users to create accounts and does not intentionally collect personally identifiable information such as:

Full name

Email address

Phone number

Government ID numbers

Unless explicitly entered by the user within the app.

2. How We Use Your Information

We use collected information to:

Manage shop inventory and sales records

Improve app functionality and performance

Fix bugs and prevent crashes

Provide customer support

3. Data Storage

All business and inventory data is stored locally on the user’s device unless cloud backup or sync is explicitly enabled.

We do not access or upload your data without your action or consent.

4. Data Sharing

We do not sell, rent, or trade user data.

Data may be shared only:

With trusted third-party services used for app analytics or crash reporting

When required by law or legal process

5. Third-Party Services

The App may use third-party services that collect information to improve app functionality, such as:

Google Play Services

Firebase Analytics

Firebase Crashlytics

These services are governed by their own privacy policies.

6. Data Security

We take reasonable measures to protect your data from unauthorized access, loss, or misuse.
However, no method of electronic storage is 100% secure.

7. User Control and Data Deletion

Users can:

Edit or delete their inventory and sales data within the app

Clear app data or uninstall the app to remove all locally stored data

For assistance, users may contact us using the details below.

8. Children’s Privacy

The App is not intended for children under the age of 13.
We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.

